## Release order (publish upstream before bumping the starter)

Publish **in dependency order** so each tarball on npm is self-consistent. Do not bump the starter until every upstream package in the chain is on npm at the new version.

| Step | Package | What must be true on npm |
|------|---------|---------------------------|
| 1 | `@spacesops/wdk-wallet-btc` | Bare addon prebuilds and `package.json` `"addon": true` versions match what pear will pack |
| 2 | `@spacesops/pear-wrk-wdk` | `generated/bundle/wdk-worklet.mobile.bundle.js` built with `bare-pack --linked`; `linked:lib…so` names match the bare addon versions you intend to ship |
| 3 | `@spacesops/react-native-bare-kit` | `libbare-kit.so` / iOS xcframework present in the tarball (`prepack` / `sync-native`); linking logic discovers nested `node_modules` addons |
| 4 | `@spacesops/wdk-react-native-core` | `dependencies` pin the new pear + bare-kit versions; `dist/` built (`prepack`) |
| 5 | **This starter** | Only `@spacesops/wdk-react-native-core@<new>` (plus lockfile); drop starter `overrides` when core pins the same bare-kit/bare-* versions |

**Alignment rule:** For every `linked:lib<name>.<version>.so` in the published pear mobile bundle, the starter install tree (after link) must produce that exact filename under `react-native-bare-kit/android/src/main/addons/<abi>/`. Fix version pins in pear / wallet-btc / bare-kit—not permanent alias scripts in the starter.

